{"type":"click","text":"C\n    \n      Shared CalendarProvider extracted from Root\n      <CalendarProvider value={...} min={...}><WeeksView weekCount={6}>...</WeeksView></CalendarProvider>\n      \n        \n          Pros\n          \n            Single source of truth for shared state — selection, min/max, locale, disabled dates defined once\n            Each view only adds its own props — clean separation of concerns\n            Both views can coexist and stay in sync automatically (shared context)\n            Forces clean factoring — shared vs view-specific logic is explicit\n            Natural extension point for future views (year view, agenda view, etc.)\n          \n        \n        \n          Cons\n          \n            Breaking change — existing <Root> API must change or become a convenience wrapper\n            More components to understand — three layers instead of one (Provider → View Root → Components)\n            Over-engineered if only two views will ever exist\n            Requires deciding upfront exactly which state is \"shared\" vs \"view-specific\" — get it wrong and you're shuffling props later","choice":"c","id":null,"timestamp":1774370851601}
